{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795137598378,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f689f2c9001il99INjQLPkeCF","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f689e7290010QeiNCdNQrk5eA","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfe46210d0f1c00d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/inbox.jsonl"},"output":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/inbox.jsonl, lines 1-3\n1: {\"id\":\"F-1-002\",\"text\":\"Operator UX: how discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview? How does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\",\"source\":\"frontier\",\"origin\":\"frontier\",\"injectedAtIteration\":0}\n2: {\"id\":\"F-1-004\",\"text\":\"Cross-CLI parity: where do cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\",\"source\":\"frontier\",\"origin\":\"frontier\",\"injectedAtIteration\":0}\n3: {\"id\":\"F-1-006\",\"text\":\"Cost and latency: what do the 8-11 minute setup, the cost per iteration, the 24-iteration ceiling and the 50/35/15 depth-band split cost in the measured runs under the spec folder's review/ and review-archive/ and the live playbook logs, and which change cuts the most time or money?\",\"source\":\"frontier\",\"origin\":\"frontier\",\"injectedAtIteration\":0}","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-en