{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795137710009,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f68ba61a001XPnu5m4oEUyuwA","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68ba056001mAzJEl7Q4t2AEI","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-917a6de95bd26813","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md && echo === && sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFrontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope .skilled/commands/deep/research.md, .skilled/commands/deep/review.md, .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt, .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt): Operator UX: how discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview? How does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n===\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] What can be deleted, merged or collapsed across runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs, both reduce-state.cjs reducers, runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs, runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs and the two workflow YAMLs while every promise stays kept?\n- [ ] How discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview, and how does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\n- [ ] Where do the cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\n- [ ] What do the 8-11 minute setup, the cost per iteration, the 24-iteration ceiling and the 50/35/15 depth-band split cost in the measured runs under the spec folder's review/ and review-archive/ and the live playbook logs, and which change cuts the most time or money?\n- [ ] Should research count stuck passes per frontier node as review now does, does the lineage completion check break resume and extend for older committed research lineages, and is there a cheap design that makes pivot admission into the frontier work?\n- [ ] How do other agentic research and code-review systems handle frontier growth, stuck detection, stop rules and multi-executor fan-out?\n- [ ] Operator UX: how discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview? How does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\n- [ ] Cross-CLI parity: where do cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\n- [ ] Cost and latency: what do the 8-11 minute setup, the cost per iteration, the 24-iteration ceiling and the 50/35/15 depth-band split cost in the measured runs under the spec folder's review/ and review-archive/ and the live playbook logs, and which change cuts the most time or money?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFrontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope .skilled/commands/deep/research.md, .skilled/commands/deep/review.md, .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt, .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt): Operator UX: how discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview? How does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n===\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] What can be deleted, merged or collapsed across runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs, both reduce-state.cjs reducers, runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs, runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs and the two workflow YAMLs while every promise stays kept?\n- [ ] How discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview, and how does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\n- [ ] Where do the cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\n- [ ] What do the 8-11 minute setup, the cost per iteration, the 24-iteration ceiling and the 50/35/15 depth-band split cost in the measured runs under the spec folder's review/ and review-archive/ and the live playbook logs, and which change cuts the most time or money?\n- [ ] Should research count stuck passes per frontier node as review now does, does the lineage completion check break resume and extend for older committed research lineages, and is there a cheap design that makes pivot admission into the frontier work?\n- [ ] How do other agentic research and code-review systems handle frontier growth, stuck detection, stop rules and multi-executor fan-out?\n- [ ] Operator UX: how discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview? How does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\n- [ ] Cross-CLI parity: where do cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\n- [ ] Cost and latency: what do the 8-11 minute setup, the cost per iteration, the 24-iteration ceiling and the 50/35/15 depth-band split cost in the measured runs under the spec folder's review/ and review-archive/ and the live playbook logs, and which change cuts the most time or money?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md && echo === && sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795137709594,"end":1795137710009}}}}
