{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795137720097,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f68bce3c001Eov8l4OjQ7mE4v","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68bc701001AdY69JXqQlnUDT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d9cc0132933cd43","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"depth-mode\\|frontier-max\\|expansive\\|--extend\\|dry-run\\|--resume\\|quota\\|429\\|rerun\" .skilled/commands/deep/review.md | head -40"},"output":"3:argument-hint: \"<target> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--frontier-max-depth=N] [--frontier-max-nodes=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run] [--restart] [--extend=N]\"\n18:  - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n41:>    - `depth_mode` (default `default` unless `--depth-mode=expansive` is present)\n43:>    - `lineage_mode` (default `auto` unless `--lineage-mode` or `--restart` is present; `--extend=N` sets `completed-continue`)\n44:>    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n100:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default` runs exactly as before. `expansive` seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes and works their next uncovered dimension, vetoing a stop while any node stays open. The frontier caps apply to a single-executor run only. See [Expansive Depth Frontier](../../skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md#expansive-depth-frontier-opt-in). |\n101:| `--frontier-max-depth` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-depth=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxDepth`, the deepest level the frontier may grow to, default `3`. Depths past 3 share the third band of `budgetSplit`. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n102:| `--frontier-max-nodes` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-nodes=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes`, the run-wide frontier node cap, which otherwise derives as half the iteration budget. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n106:| `--dry-run` | no value | See Dry-Run Flag below. |\n109:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_dimensions_clean` at once, and an expansive run whose frontier is already drained can re-stop on `frontier_drained` the same way, so create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n110:| `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n137:`--dry-run` is a first-class flag in both execution modes, not a third execution mode. It still performs real setup resolution, artifact-root resolution, focus selection, prompt rendering and convergence reads when those steps can run without side effects.\n139:With fan-out executors, `--dry-run` first runs `fanout-run.cjs --preview`. For each lineage it prints the command a real run would start: the argv with every prompt replaced by its digest, plus cwd, session id, iterations, frontier scope, the Claude config dir when set, and the model, reasoning effort, sandbox and permission mode. Runner warnings are printed too. Nothing is written to the packet. The run then halts at the first side-effect step as before.\n141:Under `--restart`, session ids come from the packet about to be archived. With `--depth-mode=expansive`, frontier scopes are empty and iterations show the unseeded default because seeding happens after the preview. A `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage shows no command. A matrix the real run would refuse prints that refusal instead. Single-executor runs and runs without `--dry-run` are unchanged.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:argument-hint: \"<target> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--frontier-max-depth=N] [--frontier-max-nodes=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run] [--restart] [--extend=N]\"\n18:  - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n41:>    - `depth_mode` (default `default` unless `--depth-mode=expansive` is present)\n43:>    - `lineage_mode` (default `auto` unless `--lineage-mode` or `--restart` is present; `--extend=N` sets `completed-continue`)\n44:>    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n100:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default` runs exactly as before. `expansive` seeds depth-1 sub-target nodes and works their next uncovered dimension, vetoing a stop while any node stays open. The frontier caps apply to a single-executor run only. See [Expansive Depth Frontier](../../skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md#expansive-depth-frontier-opt-in). |\n101:| `--frontier-max-depth` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-depth=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxDepth`, the deepest level the frontier may grow to, default `3`. Depths past 3 share the third band of `budgetSplit`. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n102:| `--frontier-max-nodes` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-nodes=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes`, the run-wide frontier node cap, which otherwise derives as half the iteration budget. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n106:| `--dry-run` | no value | See Dry-Run Flag below. |\n109:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_dimensions_clean` at once, and an expansive run whose frontier is already drained can re-stop on `frontier_drained` the same way, so create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n110:| `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n137:`--dry-run` is a first-class flag in both execution modes, not a third execution mode. It still performs real setup resolution, artifact-root resolution, focus selection, prompt rendering and convergence reads when those steps can run without side effects.\n139:With fan-out executors, `--dry-run` first runs `fanout-run.cjs --preview`. For each lineage it prints the command a real run would start: the argv with every prompt replaced by its digest, plus cwd, session id, iterations, frontier scope, the Claude config dir when set, and the model, reasoning effort, sandbox and permission mode. Runner warnings are printed too. Nothing is written to the packet. The run then halts at the first side-effect step as before.\n141:Under `--restart`, session ids come from the packet about to be archived. With `--depth-mode=expansive`, frontier scopes are empty and iterations show the unseeded default because seeding happens after the preview. A `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage shows no command. A matrix the real run would refuse prints that refusal instead. Single-executor runs and runs without `--dry-run` are unchanged.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"depth-mode\\\\|frontier-max\\\\|expansive\\\\|--extend\\\\|dry-run\\\\|--resume\\\\|quota\\\\|429\\\\|rerun\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/review.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1795137719868,"end":1795137720097}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795137720105,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f68bcd39001i815h1uK6QgVa5","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68bc701001AdY69JXqQlnUDT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-84c0f717b05d9ab1","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && wc -l .skilled/commands/deep/research.md .skilled/commands/deep/review.md .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt && echo === && grep -n \"depth-mode\\|frontier-max\\|expansive\\|--extend\\|dry-run\\|--resume\\|quota\\|429\\|rerun\" .skilled/commands/deep/research.md | head -40"},"output":"     179 .skilled/commands/deep/research.md\n     176 .skilled/commands/deep/review.md\n     448 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt\n     519 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt\n    1322 total\n===\n3:argument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--frontier-max-depth=N] [--frontier-max-nodes=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run] [--restart] [--extend=N]\"\n41:>    - `depth_mode` (default `default` unless `--depth-mode=expansive` is present)\n43:>    - `lineage_mode` (default `auto` unless `--lineage-mode` or `--restart` is present; `--extend=N` sets `completed-continue`)\n44:>    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n107:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default`, the value when the flag is absent, runs exactly as before. `expansive` is opt-in: the run seeds depth-1 frontier nodes from the topic before iteration 1, admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows as new questions under the relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order, (`expansiveDepth` in the config: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a 50/35/15 iteration budget across depths, and a run-wide `maxFrontierNodes` cap that defaults to half of `--max-iterations`), steers Next Focus to the shallowest open node, and turns a convergence stop into another iteration while frontier nodes stay open. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, the minIterations floor, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(10, 2 × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes, 16 at the full six seeds, and the seed step prints the derived budget. A fan-out lineage with no matrix `iterations` value is sized the same way from its own round-robin share of the seed, with a floor of 12 for a native lineage and 10 for a CLI one, and a lineage dealt no seed node runs at that floor. The node cap stays half that budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. Fan-out lineages each get a share of the seeded nodes. |\n108:| `--frontier-max-depth` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-depth=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxDepth`, the deepest level the frontier may grow to, default `3`. Depths past 3 share the third band of `budgetSplit`. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n109:| `--frontier-max-nodes` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-nodes=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes`, the run-wide frontier node cap, which otherwise derives as half the iteration budget. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n113:| `--dry-run` | no value | See Dry-Run Flag below. |\n116:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n117:| `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n141:`--dry-run` is a first-class flag in both execution modes, not a third execution mode. It still performs real setup resolution, artifact-root resolution, focus selection, prompt rendering, and convergence reads when those steps can run without side effects.\n143:With fan-out executors, `--dry-run` first runs `fanout-run.cjs --preview`. For each lineage it prints the command a real run would start: the argv with every prompt replaced by its digest, plus cwd, session id, iterations, frontier scope, the Claude config dir when set, and the model, reasoning effort, sandbox and permission mode. Runner warnings are printed too. Nothing is written to the packet. The run then halts at the first side-effect step as before.\n145:Under `--restart`, session ids come from the packet about to be archived. With `--depth-mode=expansive`, frontier scopes are empty and iterations show the unseeded default because seeding happens after the preview. A `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage shows no command. A matrix the real run would refuse prints that refusal instead. Single-executor runs and runs without `--dry-run` are unchanged.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"     179 .skilled/commands/deep/research.md\n     176 .skilled/commands/deep/review.md\n     448 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt\n     519 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt\n    1322 total\n===\n3:argument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--depth-mode=default|expansive] [--frontier-max-depth=N] [--frontier-max-nodes=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run] [--restart] [--extend=N]\"\n41:>    - `depth_mode` (default `default` unless `--depth-mode=expansive` is present)\n43:>    - `lineage_mode` (default `auto` unless `--lineage-mode` or `--restart` is present; `--extend=N` sets `completed-continue`)\n44:>    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n107:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default`, the value when the flag is absent, runs exactly as before. `expansive` is opt-in: the run seeds depth-1 frontier nodes from the topic before iteration 1, admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows as new questions under the relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order, (`expansiveDepth` in the config: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a 50/35/15 iteration budget across depths, and a run-wide `maxFrontierNodes` cap that defaults to half of `--max-iterations`), steers Next Focus to the shallowest open node, and turns a convergence stop into another iteration while frontier nodes stay open. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, the minIterations floor, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(10, 2 × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes, 16 at the full six seeds, and the seed step prints the derived budget. A fan-out lineage with no matrix `iterations` value is sized the same way from its own round-robin share of the seed, with a floor of 12 for a native lineage and 10 for a CLI one, and a lineage dealt no seed node runs at that floor. The node cap stays half that budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. Fan-out lineages each get a share of the seeded nodes. |\n108:| `--frontier-max-depth` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-depth=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxDepth`, the deepest level the frontier may grow to, default `3`. Depths past 3 share the third band of `budgetSplit`. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n109:| `--frontier-max-nodes` | positive integer, as `--frontier-max-nodes=N` | Sets `expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes`, the run-wide frontier node cap, which otherwise derives as half the iteration budget. Valid only with `--depth-mode=expansive` on a single-executor run; a fan-out run refuses it, because each lineage writes its own config. |\n113:| `--dry-run` | no value | See Dry-Run Flag below. |\n116:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n117:| `--extend-minutes` | positive integer, as `--extend-minutes=M` | Minutes added to the duration budget on an extension, default the prior `maxDurationMinutes`. The new budget is `max(prior, elapsed) + M`, because the clock counts idle time since `createdAt`, so an extension started after the old budget still runs. Valid only with `--extend`. |\n141:`--dry-run` is a first-class flag in both execution modes, not a third execution mode. It still performs real setup resolution, artifact-root resolution, focus selection, prompt rendering, and convergence reads when those steps can run without side effects.\n143:With fan-out executors, `--dry-run` first runs `fanout-run.cjs --preview`. For each lineage it prints the command a real run would start: the argv with every prompt replaced by its digest, plus cwd, session id, iterations, frontier scope, the Claude config dir when set, and the model, reasoning effort, sandbox and permission mode. Runner warnings are printed too. Nothing is written to the packet. The run then halts at the first side-effect step as before.\n145:Under `--restart`, session ids come from the packet about to be archived. With `--depth-mode=expansive`, frontier scopes are empty and iterations show the unseeded default because seeding happens after the preview. A `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage shows no command. A matrix the real run would refuse prints that refusal instead. Single-executor runs and runs without `--dry-run` are unchanged.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && wc -l .skilled/commands/deep/research.md .skilled/commands/deep/review.md .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt && echo === && grep -n \\\"depth-mode\\\\|frontier-max\\\\|expansive\\\\|--extend\\\\|dry-run\\\\|--resume\\\\|quota\\\\|429\\\\|rerun\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/research.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1795137719609,"end":1795137720105}}}}
