deep-research-presentation.txt:31:Under `--restart`, session ids come from the packet about to be archived. With `--depth-mode=expansive`, frontier scopes are empty and iterations show the unseeded default because seeding happens after the preview. A `cli-mistral-vibe` lineage shows no command. A matrix the real run would refuse prints that refusal instead. Single-executor runs and runs without `--dry-run` are unchanged.\n.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:49:  depth_mode: default  # default | expansive (opt-in frontier growth)\n.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:50:  frontier_scope: none  # internal, written by fan-out for an expansive lineage: comma-separated frontier node ids, or none\n.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:54:  frontier_max_depth: \"\"  # optional positive integer N from --frontier-max-depth=N, expansive depth only: expansiveDepth.maxDepth, default 3\n.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:55:  frontier_max_nodes: \"\"  # optional positive integer N from --frontier-max-nodes=N, expansive depth only: expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes, default half the iteration budget\n.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:74:| `maxIterations`         | Y        | flag `--max-iterations`, marker `maxIterations`, or default; the setup-only binding `max_iterations_source` names which (`flag`, `marker`, `setup`, `matrix` or `default`) and is never written to the config. Under `--depth-mode=expansive` a `default` budget is resized after the seed step to `min(24, max(10, 2·c·(S + maxDepth − 1)))`, with S the depth-1 nodes the seed admitted and c = 1. That is the single-executor budget: a fan-out lineage with no matrix `iterations` value is sized the same way from its own round-robin share of the open seed nodes, with maxDepth at its default of 3 and a floor of 12 native or 10 CLI, which a lineage dealt no node runs at; for a fan-out lineage only a matri