{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795137858269,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f68de966002GERXa8cQMRUGWP","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68dd7c0001vKOHxTztZFWJ4N","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-92cf186d422fad28","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"if_cli_[a-z_]*:\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | wc -l && grep -n \"if_cli_[a-z_]*:\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml | head -12 && echo === && grep -c \"if_cli_\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"      16\n1738:        if_cli_deepseek_harness:\n1752:        if_cli_mistral_vibe:\n1762:        if_cli_claude_code:\n1777:        if_cli_cursor:\n1786:        if_cli_devin:\n1795:        if_cli_pi:\n1812:        if_cli_opencode:\n1825:        if_cli_codex:\n===\n9\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      16\n1738:        if_cli_deepseek_harness:\n1752:        if_cli_mistral_vibe:\n1762:        if_cli_claude_code:\n1777:        if_cli_cursor:\n1786:        if_cli_devin:\n1795:        if_cli_pi:\n1812:        if_cli_opencode:\n1825:        if_cli_codex:\n===\n9\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"if_cli_[a-z_]*:\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | wc -l && grep -n \\\"if_cli_[a-z_]*:\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml | head -12 && echo === && grep -c \\\"if_cli_\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1795137857894,"end":1795137858269}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1795137859199,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"id":"prt_1f68dee7f001j4HSXSadsPbwF4","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68dd7c0001vKOHxTztZFWJ4N","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"51a5bb9435a787bc952595238aa294b84195ef6a","cost":0.001762024,"tokens":{"input":1021,"output":157,"reasoning":837,"cache":{"read":190656,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795137860707,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"id":"prt_1f68df4630010rr0qNLs0ytUqD","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68dee84001t58GpfaXWlWbTs","type":"step-start","snapshot":"51a5bb9435a787bc952595238aa294b84195ef6a"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795137867200,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f68df914002WEbzsdnEFJk4yu","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68dee84001t58GpfaXWlWbTs","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-828ea851a028f38b","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 2: Frontier node F-1-004 — cross-CLI parity\n\n## Focus\n\nFrontier node F-1-004 (depth 1, scope `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`): where do the eight CLI lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The \"single executor contract\" already exists as data — but only half of it is printed.** `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` (`executor-config.ts:112-142`) declares which config fields each kind accepts, and `EXECUTOR_PREVENTIVE_SANDBOX_CAPABILITY` (`:159-169`) declares whether the kind's sandbox is a real OS boundary, a compensating control, or nothing. `finalizeLineageCommand` then emits `sandboxMode` and `permissionMode` in `effectiveConfig` (`fanout-run.cjs:2507-2516`) and the preview prints exactly those two, so a `cli-pi` or `cli-devin` lineage shows `sandboxMode: workspace-write` even though the matrix says `false` (no preventive boundary). One concrete change: add `sandboxEnforcement: \"preventive\" | \"compensating\" | \"none\"` to `effectiveConfig` from the capability matrix and print it beside `sandbox` in the preview and `invocation-metadata.json`. Value: ends the \"which CLI actually confines\" question with one field. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:159] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2507]\n\n2. **`reasoningEffort` is a per-kind lottery in an otherwise shared matrix.** The Zod schema accepts it for every kind (`executor-config.ts:91`), but the supported-field table rejects it for `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin` and `cli-mistral-vibe` because those ids bake the tier into the model name (`:117-141`), so one `--executors` matrix that sets effort for all lineages fails on the three that cannot honor it. One concrete change: keep the field accepted for every kind, map it in the adapter (`--effort`, `--variant`, `--thinking`, or a `#effort` model suffix), and report `effortApplied: \"flag\" | \"baked\" | \"none\"` in `effectiveConfig`, with a loud warning when a requested tier cannot be honored. Value: one matrix works across all eight kinds. Effort M. Risk medium (a silent downgrade would be worse than the current hard failure; the warning is the contract). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:91] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:117] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2659]\n\n3. **Failure classification keeps kind-specific branches in the shared worker instead of in the adapter table.** `fanout-run.cjs:4695` ignores a non-zero exit for `cli-pi` only, `:4664-4667` runs extra completion validators for `cli-deepseek-harness` and `cli-mistral-vibe`, and `:4714` maps quota exhaustion to its own reason across all kinds. The worker therefore knows four kinds by name, and a new kind must edit it. One concrete change: let each entry in `LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS` (`:3557-3567`) carry `exitPolicy` and `completionValidator`, and have the worker classify from those fields only. Value: one failure model; new kinds add data, not branches. Effort M. Risk medium (the pi tolerance and the vibe partial verdict must move without behavior change). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3557] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4695] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4664]\n\n4. **The six per-kind single-executor branches in each YAML are the same command with a different `--executor` argument.** `deep-research.yaml:1762-1837` has eight `if_cli_*` branches; six of them (claude-code, cursor, devin, pi, opencode, codex) run `dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor <kind>` with identical arguments, and only `cli-deepseek-harness` (extra `--spec-folder`) and `cli-mistral-vibe` (fail closed) differ. `deep-review.yaml` carries the same duplication. One concrete change: collapse the six into one `if_cli` branch whose `--executor` is `{config.executor.kind}`, keep the two special branches, in both YAMLs. Value: roughly 60 lines removed per YAML and one place to add the next kind. Effort S. Risk low (`dispatch-iteration.cjs` already accepts the kind as a value). [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1762] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1812] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1738] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1752]\n\n5. **Log shape and resume are already at parity; the remaining asymmetry is `native`.** Every kind writes the same `logs/fanout-lineage.out` and `.err` with rotation (`fanout-run.cjs:4640-4645`), and every kind resumes through `readStoredLineageSessionId` (`:772`), so those two axes need no contract. But `native` is listed in `EXECUTOR_KINDS` and in `LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS`, yet `buildNativeLineageCommand` throws on OpenCode v2 by construction (`:2640-2645`), so a matrix that names `native` works or fails on the host's OpenCode major version. One concrete change: remove `native` from the fan-out adapter table and reject it in `preflightFanoutCapabilities` with the same message, or gate it behind an explicit `native-command-surface` kind. Value: removes a version-dependent trap from the matrix. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4640] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2640] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Treating log shape as a parity gap: all kinds already write the same rotated `fanout-lineage.out/.err` pair, so no change is needed there.\n- Proposing a new config schema: `executor-config.ts` is already the single schema; the gap is that two derived facts (enforcement class, effort application) are not carried into the output.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching for per-kind resume flags: resume is config-driven for every kind through `readStoredLineageSessionId`, so there is nothing to unify.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"log shape\" could mean the file pair or the JSON event shape. Read as the file pair; the event shape is already uniform through the append gateway.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: no live CLI binaries were invoked; the flag matrices and builders are the evidence.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11,91,112,117,159`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:772,2494,2507,2533,2640,2659,3557,4640,4664,4695,4714`\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1738,1752,1762,1812,1825`\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` (same branch shape)\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Questions addressed: cross-CLI parity (frontier node F-1-004)\n- Questions answered: none yet; the node stays open for the failure-class pass\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: reading the capability matrices before the workers showed that parity is mostly encoded already, which turned the question from \"invent a contract\" into \"publish the contract you have\".\n- What did not work and why: looking for per-kind resume or log differences found none; the asymmetry is concentrated in the YAML branches and the worker's kind checks.\n- What I would do differently: diff the two YAML executor sections line by line next time, since that is where the duplication is measurable.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nKeep F-1-004 open for a short pass on the failure-class table and the `native` removal, then move to F-1-006 (cost and latency) and back to F-1-002 for the partial-run summary.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 2: Frontier node F-1-004 — cross-CLI parity\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-1-004 (depth 1, scope `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`): where do the eight CLI lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **The \\\"single executor contract\\\" already exists as data — but only half of it is printed.** `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` (`executor-config.ts:112-142`) declares which config fields each kind accepts, and `EXECUTOR_PREVENTIVE_SANDBOX_CAPABILITY` (`:159-169`) declares whether the kind's sandbox is a real OS boundary, a compensating control, or nothing. `finalizeLineageCommand` then emits `sandboxMode` and `permissionMode` in `effectiveConfig` (`fanout-run.cjs:2507-2516`) and the preview prints exactly those two, so a `cli-pi` or `cli-devin` lineage shows `sandboxMode: workspace-write` even though the matrix says `false` (no preventive boundary). One concrete change: add `sandboxEnforcement: \\\"preventive\\\" | \\\"compensating\\\" | \\\"none\\\"` to `effectiveConfig` from the capability matrix and print it beside `sandbox` in the preview and `invocation-metadata.json`. Value: ends the \\\"which CLI actually confines\\\" question with one field. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:159] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2507]\\n\\n2. **`reasoningEffort` is a per-kind lottery in an otherwise shared matrix.** The Zod schema accepts it for every kind (`executor-config.ts:91`), but the supported-field table rejects it for `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin` and `cli-mistral-vibe` because those ids bake the tier into the model name (`:117-141`), so one `--executors` matrix that sets effort for all lineages fails on the three that cannot honor it. One concrete change: keep the field accepted for every kind, map it in the adapter (`--effort`, `--variant`, `--thinking`, or a `#effort` model suffix), and report `effortApplied: \\\"flag\\\" | \\\"baked\\\" | \\\"none\\\"` in `effectiveConfig`, with a loud warning when a requested tier cannot be honored. Value: one matrix works across all eight kinds. Effort M. Risk medium (a silent downgrade would be worse than the current hard failure; the warning is the contract). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:91] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:117] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2659]\\n\\n3. **Failure classification keeps kind-specific branches in the shared worker instead of in the adapter table.** `fanout-run.cjs:4695` ignores a non-zero exit for `cli-pi` only, `:4664-4667` runs extra completion validators for `cli-deepseek-harness` and `cli-mistral-vibe`, and `:4714` maps quota exhaustion to its own reason across all kinds. The worker therefore knows four kinds by name, and a new kind must edit it. One concrete change: let each entry in `LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS` (`:3557-3567`) carry `exitPolicy` and `completionValidator`, and have the worker classify from those fields only. Value: one failure model; new kinds add data, not branches. Effort M. Risk medium (the pi tolerance and the vibe partial verdict must move without behavior change). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3557] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4695] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4664]\\n\\n4. **The six per-kind single-executor branches in each YAML are the same command with a different `--executor` argument.** `deep-research.yaml:1762-1837` has eight `if_cli_*` branches; six of them (claude-code, cursor, devin, pi, opencode, codex) run `dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor <kind>` with identical arguments, and only `cli-deepseek-harness` (extra `--spec-folder`) and `cli-mistral-vibe` (fail closed) differ. `deep-review.yaml` carries the same duplication. One concrete change: collapse the six into one `if_cli` branch whose `--executor` is `{config.executor.kind}`, keep the two special branches, in both YAMLs. Value: roughly 60 lines removed per YAML and one place to add the next kind. Effort S. Risk low (`dispatch-iteration.cjs` already accepts the kind as a value). [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1762] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1812] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1738] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1752]\\n\\n5. **Log shape and resume are already at parity; the remaining asymmetry is `native`.** Every kind writes the same `logs/fanout-lineage.out` and `.err` with rotation (`fanout-run.cjs:4640-4645`), and every kind resumes through `readStoredLineageSessionId` (`:772`), so those two axes need no contract. But `native` is listed in `EXECUTOR_KINDS` and in `LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS`, yet `buildNativeLineageCommand` throws on OpenCode v2 by construction (`:2640-2645`), so a matrix that names `native` works or fails on the host's OpenCode major version. One concrete change: remove `native` from the fan-out adapter table and reject it in `preflightFanoutCapabilities` with the same message, or gate it behind an explicit `native-command-surface` kind. Value: removes a version-dependent trap from the matrix. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4640] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2640] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Treating log shape as a parity gap: all kinds already write the same rotated `fanout-lineage.out/.err` pair, so no change is needed there.\\n- Proposing a new config schema: `executor-config.ts` is already the single schema; the gap is that two derived facts (enforcement class, effort application) are not carried into the output.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Searching for per-kind resume flags: resume is config-driven for every kind through `readStoredLineageSessionId`, so there is nothing to unify.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"log shape\\\" could mean the file pair or the JSON event shape. Read as the file pair; the event shape is already uniform through the append gateway.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\\n- Missing dependencies: no live CLI binaries were invoked; the flag matrices and builders are the evidence.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11,91,112,117,159`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:772,2494,2507,2533,2640,2659,3557,4640,4664,4695,4714`\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1738,1752,1762,1812,1825`\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml` (same branch shape)\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 1.0\\n- Questions addressed: cross-CLI parity (frontier node F-1-004)\\n- Questions answered: none yet; the node stays open for the failure-class pass\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: reading the capability matrices before the workers showed that parity is mostly encoded already, which turned the question from \\\"invent a contract\\\" into \\\"publish the contract you have\\\".\\n- What did not work and why: looking for per-kind resume or log differences found none; the asymmetry is concentrated in the YAML branches and the worker's kind checks.\\n- What I would do differently: diff the two YAML executor sections line by line next time, since that is where the duplication is measurable.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nKeep F-1-004 open for a short pass on the failure-class table and the `native` removal, then move to F-1-006 (cost and latency) and back to F-1-002 for the partial-run summary.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795137861908,"end":1795137867200}}}}
