{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795137911834,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"id":"prt_1f68ebc1a001pLCQ3dzZBoe2wB","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68eb5cc001qdNKJvvd0WtcWM","type":"step-start","snapshot":"e0c14e29a5e44f50a656606d1573654a8ba9676d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795137920482,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f68ec419002Va0pHhOlAU6MEL","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68eb5cc001qdNKJvvd0WtcWM","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a985a9e79ce46ff","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 3: Frontier node F-1-006 — cost and latency\n\n## Focus\n\nFrontier node F-1-006 (depth 1, scope `review/` and `review-archive/`): what do the 8-11 minute setup, the cost per iteration, the 24-iteration ceiling and the 50/35/15 depth-band split cost in the measured runs and the live playbook logs, and which change cuts the most time or money?\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The 24-iteration ceiling is unreachable at the measured 8-11 minutes per iteration under the default 120-minute duration budget; the duration stop binds first.** The review protocol already admits it (\"At about seven to eight minutes an iteration, a 24-iteration review can reach `maxDurationMinutes` (120) before its iteration cap\"), and one committed archive run shows the operator's workaround: `review-archive/20261119T153733Z` raised `maxDurationMinutes` to 360 for 10 iterations. At 8-11 min/iteration, 120 minutes funds 11-15 iterations, not 24, so the advertised cap is not the effective one. One concrete change: at config creation, derive the default duration budget from the iteration cap (`max(120, 10 × maxIterations)` for review, `max(120, 12 × maxIterations)` for research) or print a one-line warning that names the iteration at which the duration stop will bind. Value: the cap an operator reads is the cap the run can reach. Effort S. Risk low (an explicit `--max-duration`/config value still wins). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:464] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-expansive-research-two-node-frontier.md:34] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T153733Z/deep-review-config.json:1]\n\n2. **Setup costs 3-10 minutes per lineage before iteration 1, and a fan-out pays it once per lineage.** Measured from config `createdAt` to the first iteration timestamp: opus 3 min, deepseek 4 min, the 10-iteration archive run 10 min, the 3-iteration archive run 6 min. The root has already resolved the topic, seeded the frontier and partitioned it before spawning, so most of that work is repeated inside each child. One concrete change: when `fanout_lineage_artifact_dir` is bound, skip the context-ladder ripgrep and the resource-map scan in the child and read the root's prepared `prior_context`/seed files instead; keep the config, strategy and registry creation because those are lineage-owned. Value: 3-9 minutes saved per lineage on a 3-lineage fan-out. Effort M. Risk medium (a lineage that starts without its own context summary must still render a valid prompt). [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/opus/deep-review-config.json:1] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T153733Z/deep-review-state.jsonl:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:117]\n\n3. **The 50/35/15 split starves the depth-1 band on a review: with three nodes per lineage and four dimensions each, depth 1 needs 12 of 24 iterations, exactly its 50% share, leaving no room for growth.** `applyBandBudget` closes every open node in a band once `spent >= cap × share` (`frontier-admit.cjs:360-395`), and the review protocol tells the operator to set `--max-iterations` to at least `2 × ceil(nodes/lineages) × dimensions` — i.e. to double the budget so the fixed 50% happens to cover depth 1. One concrete change: size `budgetSplit.depth1` from the seed (`nodesPerLineage × dimensions / maxIterations`, capped at 0.7) and give the remainder to depth 2 and 3, instead of a fixed 0.5. Value: a wide review funds its seeds before it funds growth, without operator arithmetic. Effort M. Risk medium-high (it changes when budget closes fire; the existing split must remain the default for default-mode runs). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:360] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:464]\n\n4. **Per-iteration cost is dominated by cache re-read of the same context, not by output.** The live playbooks measure 0.33M input, 0.03M output and 6.2M cache-read tokens for one added iteration, and 0.57M-0.75M input with 11.9M-13.7M cache-read over three iterations; at 24 iterations that is roughly 8M input and 150M cache-read. The prompt pack restates the full research topic and the whole state summary every iteration (`prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:12-19`), which is exactly the re-read. One concrete change: render the topic as a path plus a one-line digest in the per-iteration pack (the leaf already reads `deep-research-config.json`), and keep only the delta summary for the last three iterations. Value: the cheapest cut in the whole budget, because it removes repeated input on every iteration. Effort S. Risk low (the leaf reads the config anyway). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-extend-expansive-research-run.md:34] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-expansive-research-two-node-frontier.md:34] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:12]\n\n5. **No host-measured duration reaches the iteration record, so every latency claim rests on model-written timestamps that mix queue, model and idle time.** The fan-out runner already computes `slotDurationMs` and the dispatch receipt carries it (`fanout-run.cjs:4058`), but the iteration row has no `durationMs`; this lineage's own rows have none, and the archive spans (10 iterations in 31 min, 3 in 36 min) cannot be separated into model time and queue time. One concrete change: stamp the host-measured `durationMs` (and `slotDurationMs` when present) onto the iteration row before the gateway append, or require it in the prompt pack's OUTPUT CONTRACT. Value: makes the cost question answerable per iteration instead of per run. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4058] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:67] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T183614Z/deep-review-state.jsonl:1]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Treating model price as the main lever: the measured cost is dominated by cache-read of unchanged context and by wall-clock latency, not by output tokens, so a cheaper model changes the multiplier, not the shape.\n- Blaming fan-out concurrency for the 429: the review run used concurrency 2 and the quota failure hit one lineage; the recovery gap is the real defect, and iteration 1 already records it.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching for a measured setup time in the playbooks: the only figure recorded is per-iteration cost, so setup had to be measured from the committed `createdAt` and first-iteration timestamps.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"8-11 minute setup\" has two evidenced readings. Both are reported: setup 3-10 min per lineage (measured from the committed runs) and per-iteration 8-11 min (playbooks). Neither reading is silently chosen as the only one.\n- Contradictory evidence: none; the 24-vs-120 tension is stated by the protocol itself and reproduced by the archive config.\n- Missing dependencies: no OpenAI/Anthropic billing export; token counts come from the playbook logs.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:464`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-extend-expansive-research-run.md:34`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-expansive-research-two-node-frontier.md:34`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-expansive-review-two-node-frontier.md:34`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:360`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4058`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:12,67`\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/opus/deep-review-config.json:1`\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T153733Z/deep-review-config.json:1`\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T183614Z/deep-review-state.jsonl:1`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Questions addressed: cost and latency (frontier node F-1-006)\n- Questions answered: none yet; the node stays open for the duration-budget pass\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: measuring `createdAt` against the first iteration timestamp turned \"setup feels slow\" into a 3-10 minute range, and reading the playbook token rows exposed cache-read as the dominant term.\n- What did not work and why: the playbooks do not separate setup from iteration time, so the two readings of \"8-11 minute\" had to be reported side by side.\n- What I would do differently: pull `slotDurationMs` from the dispatch receipts for the archive runs before asserting any per-iteration latency.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nClose F-1-006 after one verification pass on the dispatch receipts, then return to F-1-002 for the partial-run summary and open F-1-005 on the design questions.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 3: Frontier node F-1-006 — cost and latency\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-1-006 (depth 1, scope `review/` and `review-archive/`): what do the 8-11 minute setup, the cost per iteration, the 24-iteration ceiling and the 50/35/15 depth-band split cost in the measured runs and the live playbook logs, and which change cuts the most time or money?\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **The 24-iteration ceiling is unreachable at the measured 8-11 minutes per iteration under the default 120-minute duration budget; the duration stop binds first.** The review protocol already admits it (\\\"At about seven to eight minutes an iteration, a 24-iteration review can reach `maxDurationMinutes` (120) before its iteration cap\\\"), and one committed archive run shows the operator's workaround: `review-archive/20261119T153733Z` raised `maxDurationMinutes` to 360 for 10 iterations. At 8-11 min/iteration, 120 minutes funds 11-15 iterations, not 24, so the advertised cap is not the effective one. One concrete change: at config creation, derive the default duration budget from the iteration cap (`max(120, 10 × maxIterations)` for review, `max(120, 12 × maxIterations)` for research) or print a one-line warning that names the iteration at which the duration stop will bind. Value: the cap an operator reads is the cap the run can reach. Effort S. Risk low (an explicit `--max-duration`/config value still wins). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:464] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-expansive-research-two-node-frontier.md:34] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T153733Z/deep-review-config.json:1]\\n\\n2. **Setup costs 3-10 minutes per lineage before iteration 1, and a fan-out pays it once per lineage.** Measured from config `createdAt` to the first iteration timestamp: opus 3 min, deepseek 4 min, the 10-iteration archive run 10 min, the 3-iteration archive run 6 min. The root has already resolved the topic, seeded the frontier and partitioned it before spawning, so most of that work is repeated inside each child. One concrete change: when `fanout_lineage_artifact_dir` is bound, skip the context-ladder ripgrep and the resource-map scan in the child and read the root's prepared `prior_context`/seed files instead; keep the config, strategy and registry creation because those are lineage-owned. Value: 3-9 minutes saved per lineage on a 3-lineage fan-out. Effort M. Risk medium (a lineage that starts without its own context summary must still render a valid prompt). [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/opus/deep-review-config.json:1] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T153733Z/deep-review-state.jsonl:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:117]\\n\\n3. **The 50/35/15 split starves the depth-1 band on a review: with three nodes per lineage and four dimensions each, depth 1 needs 12 of 24 iterations, exactly its 50% share, leaving no room for growth.** `applyBandBudget` closes every open node in a band once `spent >= cap × share` (`frontier-admit.cjs:360-395`), and the review protocol tells the operator to set `--max-iterations` to at least `2 × ceil(nodes/lineages) × dimensions` — i.e. to double the budget so the fixed 50% happens to cover depth 1. One concrete change: size `budgetSplit.depth1` from the seed (`nodesPerLineage × dimensions / maxIterations`, capped at 0.7) and give the remainder to depth 2 and 3, instead of a fixed 0.5. Value: a wide review funds its seeds before it funds growth, without operator arithmetic. Effort M. Risk medium-high (it changes when budget closes fire; the existing split must remain the default for default-mode runs). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:360] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:464]\\n\\n4. **Per-iteration cost is dominated by cache re-read of the same context, not by output.** The live playbooks measure 0.33M input, 0.03M output and 6.2M cache-read tokens for one added iteration, and 0.57M-0.75M input with 11.9M-13.7M cache-read over three iterations; at 24 iterations that is roughly 8M input and 150M cache-read. The prompt pack restates the full research topic and the whole state summary every iteration (`prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:12-19`), which is exactly the re-read. One concrete change: render the topic as a path plus a one-line digest in the per-iteration pack (the leaf already reads `deep-research-config.json`), and keep only the delta summary for the last three iterations. Value: the cheapest cut in the whole budget, because it removes repeated input on every iteration. Effort S. Risk low (the leaf reads the config anyway). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-extend-expansive-research-run.md:34] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-expansive-research-two-node-frontier.md:34] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:12]\\n\\n5. **No host-measured duration reaches the iteration record, so every latency claim rests on model-written timestamps that mix queue, model and idle time.** The fan-out runner already computes `slotDurationMs` and the dispatch receipt carries it (`fanout-run.cjs:4058`), but the iteration row has no `durationMs`; this lineage's own rows have none, and the archive spans (10 iterations in 31 min, 3 in 36 min) cannot be separated into model time and queue time. One concrete change: stamp the host-measured `durationMs` (and `slotDurationMs` when present) onto the iteration row before the gateway append, or require it in the prompt pack's OUTPUT CONTRACT. Value: makes the cost question answerable per iteration instead of per run. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4058] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:67] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T183614Z/deep-review-state.jsonl:1]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Treating model price as the main lever: the measured cost is dominated by cache-read of unchanged context and by wall-clock latency, not by output tokens, so a cheaper model changes the multiplier, not the shape.\\n- Blaming fan-out concurrency for the 429: the review run used concurrency 2 and the quota failure hit one lineage; the recovery gap is the real defect, and iteration 1 already records it.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Searching for a measured setup time in the playbooks: the only figure recorded is per-iteration cost, so setup had to be measured from the committed `createdAt` and first-iteration timestamps.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"8-11 minute setup\\\" has two evidenced readings. Both are reported: setup 3-10 min per lineage (measured from the committed runs) and per-iteration 8-11 min (playbooks). Neither reading is silently chosen as the only one.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none; the 24-vs-120 tension is stated by the protocol itself and reproduced by the archive config.\\n- Missing dependencies: no OpenAI/Anthropic billing export; token counts come from the playbook logs.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:464`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-extend-expansive-research-run.md:34`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-expansive-research-two-node-frontier.md:34`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/entry-points-and-modes/live-expansive-review-two-node-frontier.md:34`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:360`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4058`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:12,67`\\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/lineages/opus/deep-review-config.json:1`\\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T153733Z/deep-review-config.json:1`\\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review-archive/20261119T183614Z/deep-review-state.jsonl:1`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 1.0\\n- Questions addressed: cost and latency (frontier node F-1-006)\\n- Questions answered: none yet; the node stays open for the duration-budget pass\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: measuring `createdAt` against the first iteration timestamp turned \\\"setup feels slow\\\" into a 3-10 minute range, and reading the playbook token rows exposed cache-read as the dominant term.\\n- What did not work and why: the playbooks do not separate setup from iteration time, so the two readings of \\\"8-11 minute\\\" had to be reported side by side.\\n- What I would do differently: pull `slotDurationMs` from the dispatch receipts for the archive runs before asserting any per-iteration latency.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nClose F-1-006 after one verification pass on the dispatch receipts, then return to F-1-002 for the partial-run summary and open F-1-005 on the design questions.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795137913881,"end":1795137920482}}}}
