{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795137958863,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"id":"prt_1f68f73cf001KiBSu0rlR0Ru5b","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68f6c82001JBKBUlQvPlXXlX","type":"step-start","snapshot":"be295e14719723ec19f5f5e3dbc7a49c51eaa407"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795137962161,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f68f7fa100145rMwA92bFjQgM","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f68f6c82001JBKBUlQvPlXXlX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9737809162fb24c3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"resume\\|recover\\|failed lineage\\|quota\" .skilled/commands/deep/research.md | head -20; echo ===; sed -n '105,120p' specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md"},"output":"107:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default`, the value when the flag is absent, runs exactly as before. `expansive` is opt-in: the run seeds depth-1 frontier nodes from the topic before iteration 1, admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows as new questions under the relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order, (`expansiveDepth` in the config: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a 50/35/15 iteration budget across depths, and a run-wide `maxFrontierNodes` cap that defaults to half of `--max-iterations`), steers Next Focus to the shallowest open node, and turns a convergence stop into another iteration while frontier nodes stay open. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, the minIterations floor, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(10, 2 × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes, 16 at the full six seeds, and the seed step prints the derived budget. A fan-out lineage with no matrix `iterations` value is sized the same way from its own round-robin share of the seed, with a floor of 12 for a native lineage and 10 for a CLI one, and a lineage dealt no seed node runs at that floor. The node cap stays half that budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. Fan-out lineages each get a share of the seeded nodes. |\n115:| `--lineage-mode` | `auto` \\| `resume` \\| `restart` | Session lifecycle intent, default `auto`. `resume` keeps the same `sessionId` and archives nothing. `restart` opens a new `sessionId` at generation+1 and archives the prior `research/`. `fork` is not accepted. |\n116:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n===\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergent-pivots -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:frontier -->\n## 6B. FRONTIER\n- Frontier size: 3 nodes (3 open, 0 active, 0 answered, 0 exhausted, 0 blocked, 0 abstained)\n- Pruned nodes: 0\n- Revisits: 0\n- Budget depth1: 3 of 5 iterations spent\n- Budget depth2: 0 of 3.5 iterations spent\n- Budget depth3: 0 of 5 iterations spent\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:frontier -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 7. NEXT FOCUS\nFrontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope .skilled/commands/deep/research.md, .skilled/commands/deep/review.md, .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt, .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt): Operator UX: how discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview? How does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"107:| `--depth-mode` | `default` \\| `expansive` | `default`, the value when the flag is absent, runs exactly as before. `expansive` is opt-in: the run seeds depth-1 frontier nodes from the topic before iteration 1, admits leaf `frontier_proposal` rows as new questions under the relevance, dedupe, depth, fan-out, budget and cycle checks, in that order, (`expansiveDepth` in the config: `maxDepth` 3, `maxChildrenPerNode` 6, a 50/35/15 iteration budget across depths, and a run-wide `maxFrontierNodes` cap that defaults to half of `--max-iterations`), steers Next Focus to the shallowest open node, and turns a convergence stop into another iteration while frontier nodes stay open. It never outranks the iteration cap, consecutive failures, the minIterations floor, stuck recovery, pause, the max-duration stop, `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. When `--max-iterations` is left at its default, the run sizes its budget from the seed: `min(24, max(10, 2 × (S + maxDepth − 1)))` iterations for S seeded depth-1 nodes, 16 at the full six seeds, and the seed step prints the derived budget. A fan-out lineage with no matrix `iterations` value is sized the same way from its own round-robin share of the seed, with a floor of 12 for a native lineage and 10 for a CLI one, and a lineage dealt no seed node runs at that floor. The node cap stays half that budget, which leaves room for at least two nodes past depth 1. An explicit `--max-iterations`, marker, setup answer or fan-out matrix `iterations` value always wins, even below the derived value, and the seed warns when it leaves no room past depth 1. Fan-out lineages each get a share of the seeded nodes. |\n115:| `--lineage-mode` | `auto` \\| `resume` \\| `restart` | Session lifecycle intent, default `auto`. `resume` keeps the same `sessionId` and archives nothing. `restart` opens a new `sessionId` at generation+1 and archives the prior `research/`. `fork` is not accepted. |\n116:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n===\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergent-pivots -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:frontier -->\n## 6B. FRONTIER\n- Frontier size: 3 nodes (3 open, 0 active, 0 answered, 0 exhausted, 0 blocked, 0 abstained)\n- Pruned nodes: 0\n- Revisits: 0\n- Budget depth1: 3 of 5 iterations spent\n- Budget depth2: 0 of 3.5 iterations spent\n- Budget depth3: 0 of 5 iterations spent\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:frontier -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 7. NEXT FOCUS\nFrontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope .skilled/commands/deep/research.md, .skilled/commands/deep/review.md, .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt, .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt): Operator UX: how discoverable are the expansive-depth flags and defaults, how is the budget sized, and how clear are the warnings, dashboards, reports and the fan-out dry-run preview? How does an operator recover mid-run from a provider quota failure, resume, extend, or rerun one failed lineage?\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"resume\\\\|recover\\\\|failed lineage\\\\|quota\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/research.md | head -20; echo ===; sed -n '105,120p' specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795137961889,"end":1795137962161}}}}
