{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795138038792,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"id":"prt_1f690ac080016a5RFhwsTzg4oh","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f690a48d001YQZFIIr41myCkT","type":"step-start","snapshot":"8202cfe5b5d9c456b9d4a15ae3a75d4e36178703"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795138043704,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f690ae150026Z6bwObAB8W0vb","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f690a48d001YQZFIIr41myCkT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f9b6415e3704aaf","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: Frontier node F-1-004 (second pass) — single-executor parity and the collapse\n\n## Focus\n\nFrontier node F-1-004, second pass: verify the single-executor dispatch path against the fan-out adapter table, and confirm the six duplicated YAML branches can collapse into one.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The claude single-executor path disagrees with itself by loop type: a review hardcodes `--permission-mode acceptEdits`, a research run resolves the mode from `sandboxMode`.** `dispatch-iteration.cjs:373` passes the literal `acceptEdits` in the review branch, while the research branch at `:423` calls `resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode)`. The fan-out adapter maps `danger-full-access` to `bypassPermissions` for both loops, and `fanout-run.cjs:1255` already warns that acceptEdits cannot run Bash non-interactively, so a `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` claude review silently cannot run the append gateway. One concrete change: replace the literal with `resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode)` in the review branch. Value: the same flag behaves the same way in both loops. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:373] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:423] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1255]\n\n2. **The six-branch collapse is verified: `dispatch-iteration.cjs` already reads `--executor` as a value and validates it against `EXECUTOR_KINDS`.** `:55-61` parses the raw flag and refuses an unknown kind before any module loads; `:214-229` adds only the claude `--claude-config-dir` and dsh `--spec-folder` constraints. So one `if_cli` branch with `--executor \"{config.executor.kind}\"` covers claude-code, cursor, devin, pi, opencode and codex in both YAMLs; the per-kind notes (`deep-research.yaml:1772-1776`, `:1819-1824`) restate the `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` matrix and can be deleted with them. Value: roughly 60 lines plus 40 lines of notes removed per YAML, one place to add the next kind. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:55] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:214] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1772] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1819]\n\n3. **The Flash top-tier effort pin is implemented twice, verbatim.** `executor-config.ts:328-337` exports `isFlashMaxPinnedModel` and `pinReasoningEffortForModel`, and `fanout-run.cjs:2650-2668` re-implements both with a \"Mirrors …\" comment so the synchronous builders do not wait on the TS loader. `fanout-run.cjs` already imports several helpers from `executor-config.ts` at load time, so the copy can be replaced by the import. One concrete change: import the two functions and delete the local pair. Value: one rule for which models are pinned to `max`. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:328] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2650]\n\n4. **`runLineageBuiltin` forces `workspace-write` for cursor, devin and pi, so a configured `read-only` request is silently upgraded to a writable run.** `dispatch-iteration.cjs:459-468` sets `const sandboxMode = 'workspace-write'` and passes it to `buildLineageCommand` for all three kinds, discarding `context.sandboxMode`. The fan-out path resolves the requested sandbox and fails closed when a kind cannot honor it (`fanout-run.cjs:3963-3966`, `:2501-2506`). One concrete change: pass the configured sandbox and let `buildLineageCommand` refuse an unhonorable request, as it already does for `cli-opencode`. Value: a confinement request is never silently widened. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:459] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2501]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Claiming the six YAML branches need different arguments: only claude (config dir) and dsh (spec folder) add a flag, and both are already optional in the shared script.\n- Treating the forced `workspace-write` as a bug in the builder: the builder honors what it is given; the silent narrowing happens in the caller.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for a review-specific claude builder in the fan-out path: there is one builder for both loops, which is exactly why the single-executor branch diverged unnoticed.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"failure classes\" could mean the summary's counts or the per-kind tolerances. Read as both; the summary counts are already uniform, and the tolerances are the adapter-table finding from iteration 2.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: no live claude review run was dispatched; the mismatch is read from the two argument builders.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:55,214,373,423,459`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1255,2501,2650,3963`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:328`\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1772,1819`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Questions addressed: cross-CLI parity (frontier node F-1-004), second pass\n- Questions answered: the parity node is answered: permissions diverge by loop type, the YAML duplicates are collapsible, the effort pin is duplicated, and the write sandbox is silently widened for three kinds.\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: comparing the two claude branches line by line found the permission mismatch, which no matrix could reveal because both branches claim to honor `sandboxMode`.\n- What did not work and why: the failure-class pass found no new class beyond iteration 2, so the finding was folded into the adapter-table recommendation instead of restated.\n- What I would do differently: diff the single-executor and fan-out builders for every kind, not only claude; the same drift may exist elsewhere.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nClose F-1-004 as answered. Next: F-1-006 receipt verification, then the design questions and restraint pass.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 5: Frontier node F-1-004 (second pass) — single-executor parity and the collapse\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-1-004, second pass: verify the single-executor dispatch path against the fan-out adapter table, and confirm the six duplicated YAML branches can collapse into one.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **The claude single-executor path disagrees with itself by loop type: a review hardcodes `--permission-mode acceptEdits`, a research run resolves the mode from `sandboxMode`.** `dispatch-iteration.cjs:373` passes the literal `acceptEdits` in the review branch, while the research branch at `:423` calls `resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode)`. The fan-out adapter maps `danger-full-access` to `bypassPermissions` for both loops, and `fanout-run.cjs:1255` already warns that acceptEdits cannot run Bash non-interactively, so a `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` claude review silently cannot run the append gateway. One concrete change: replace the literal with `resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode)` in the review branch. Value: the same flag behaves the same way in both loops. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:373] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:423] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1255]\\n\\n2. **The six-branch collapse is verified: `dispatch-iteration.cjs` already reads `--executor` as a value and validates it against `EXECUTOR_KINDS`.** `:55-61` parses the raw flag and refuses an unknown kind before any module loads; `:214-229` adds only the claude `--claude-config-dir` and dsh `--spec-folder` constraints. So one `if_cli` branch with `--executor \\\"{config.executor.kind}\\\"` covers claude-code, cursor, devin, pi, opencode and codex in both YAMLs; the per-kind notes (`deep-research.yaml:1772-1776`, `:1819-1824`) restate the `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` matrix and can be deleted with them. Value: roughly 60 lines plus 40 lines of notes removed per YAML, one place to add the next kind. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:55] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:214] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1772] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1819]\\n\\n3. **The Flash top-tier effort pin is implemented twice, verbatim.** `executor-config.ts:328-337` exports `isFlashMaxPinnedModel` and `pinReasoningEffortForModel`, and `fanout-run.cjs:2650-2668` re-implements both with a \\\"Mirrors …\\\" comment so the synchronous builders do not wait on the TS loader. `fanout-run.cjs` already imports several helpers from `executor-config.ts` at load time, so the copy can be replaced by the import. One concrete change: import the two functions and delete the local pair. Value: one rule for which models are pinned to `max`. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:328] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2650]\\n\\n4. **`runLineageBuiltin` forces `workspace-write` for cursor, devin and pi, so a configured `read-only` request is silently upgraded to a writable run.** `dispatch-iteration.cjs:459-468` sets `const sandboxMode = 'workspace-write'` and passes it to `buildLineageCommand` for all three kinds, discarding `context.sandboxMode`. The fan-out path resolves the requested sandbox and fails closed when a kind cannot honor it (`fanout-run.cjs:3963-3966`, `:2501-2506`). One concrete change: pass the configured sandbox and let `buildLineageCommand` refuse an unhonorable request, as it already does for `cli-opencode`. Value: a confinement request is never silently widened. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:459] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2501]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Claiming the six YAML branches need different arguments: only claude (config dir) and dsh (spec folder) add a flag, and both are already optional in the shared script.\\n- Treating the forced `workspace-write` as a bug in the builder: the builder honors what it is given; the silent narrowing happens in the caller.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for a review-specific claude builder in the fan-out path: there is one builder for both loops, which is exactly why the single-executor branch diverged unnoticed.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"failure classes\\\" could mean the summary's counts or the per-kind tolerances. Read as both; the summary counts are already uniform, and the tolerances are the adapter-table finding from iteration 2.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\\n- Missing dependencies: no live claude review run was dispatched; the mismatch is read from the two argument builders.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:55,214,373,423,459`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1255,2501,2650,3963`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:328`\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1772,1819`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 1.0\\n- Questions addressed: cross-CLI parity (frontier node F-1-004), second pass\\n- Questions answered: the parity node is answered: permissions diverge by loop type, the YAML duplicates are collapsible, the effort pin is duplicated, and the write sandbox is silently widened for three kinds.\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: comparing the two claude branches line by line found the permission mismatch, which no matrix could reveal because both branches claim to honor `sandboxMode`.\\n- What did not work and why: the failure-class pass found no new class beyond iteration 2, so the finding was folded into the adapter-table recommendation instead of restated.\\n- What I would do differently: diff the single-executor and fan-out builders for every kind, not only claude; the same drift may exist elsewhere.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nClose F-1-004 as answered. Next: F-1-006 receipt verification, then the design questions and restraint pass.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795138039317,"end":1795138043704}}}}
