{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795138050484,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f690ce9c002IXy2ZnJ48a3Ik0","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f690c3140018m550YUh84yfTb","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f68f8eee58416dd","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":5,\"runId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1795137583671-xybhyk\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1795137583671-xybhyk\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1795137583671-xybhyk\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":5,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Frontier node F-1-004 (depth 1, scope .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts): Cross-CLI parity: where do cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\",\"findingsCount\":4,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Four new findings: one surfaced permission mismatch, one verified collapse, one duplicated pin, one silent sandbox widening.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Cross-CLI parity: where do cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Cross-CLI parity: where do cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe lineages still differ in permissions, effort flags, failure classes, resume and log shape, and what single executor contract would remove the differences?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"The six YAML branches needing different arguments\",\"The forced workspace-write as a builder bug\"],\"focusTrack\":\"parity\",\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:373\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:459\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2650\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:328\"],\"graphEvents\":[]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-001\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"label\":\"The claude single-executor review branch hardcodes --permission-mode acceptEdits while the research branch resolves it from sandboxMode, so the same danger-full-access flag yields a review that cannot run Bash or the append gateway.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:373\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:423\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1255\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-002\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"label\":\"The six-branch collapse is verified: dispatch-iteration.cjs parses --executor as a value and validates it against EXECUTOR_KINDS, so one if_cli branch plus the claude and dsh optional flags covers six kinds in both YAMLs.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:55\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:214\",\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1772\",\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:1819\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-003\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"label\":\"The Flash top-tier effort pin is implemented verbatim twice, in executor-config.ts:328-337 and fanout-run.cjs:2650-2668; fanout-run already imports from executor-config, so the mirror can be an import.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:328\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2650\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-004\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"label\":\"runLineageBuiltin forces workspace-write for cursor, devin and pi and discards the configured sandbox, so a read-only request is silently widened instead of refused like cli-opencode.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:459\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2501\"]}\n{\"type\":\"frontier_proposal\",\"parentId\":\"F-1-004\",\"question\":\"Does the single-executor builder drift from the fan-out adapter for codex, cursor, devin or pi the way the claude review branch does, and can one shared argument builder remove the drift for every kind?\",\"scope\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs\",\"evidence\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:373\"}\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-005.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-005.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deltas/iter-005.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\