{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795138095067,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f69176b4002IUqoD8jXf5KwFx","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f6916abd001YOD11lsc2tSmhX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab44147ead9cf478","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 6: Frontier node F-2-007 — what a partial fan-out tells the operator\n\n## Focus\n\nFrontier node F-2-007 (depth 2, child of F-1-002): does a partially complete fan-out summary name the failed lineage, its failure class and the exact command to rerun just that lineage?\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **A partial fan-out never reaches synthesis, so the successful lineages are never merged into a report.** `fanout-run.cjs:4969` exits `3` when every lineage failed and `2` when some failed; `deep-research.yaml`'s `step_fanout_spawn` has no `on_failure` branch and its next instruction is \"After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis\" (`:432`). One failed lane therefore stops the parent before `step_fanout_merge`, and the operator gets complete per-lineage artifacts but no consolidated `research.md` or registry. One concrete change: exit `0` with `status: \"partial\"` (or add `--allow-partial`) when at least one lineage succeeded, and let `phase_synthesis` merge what exists with a banner naming the failed labels. Value: a 2-of-3 fan-out still produces the deliverable it already paid for. Effort M. Risk medium (a partial merge must never read as complete coverage; the banner and summary counters are the guard). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4969] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:432] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:2073]\n\n2. **The per-lineage result already exists and is thrown away when the summary is written.** `buildPoolSummary` returns `{results, summary}` (`fanout-pool.cjs:977-1001`), and each result carries the lane output and its failure object; `writeOrchestrationSummary` serializes only the aggregate summary plus the fanout-specific fields, which is why the committed `orchestration-summary.json` has counts but no labels. One concrete change: write a reduced `lineages: [{label, status, reason, failure_class, exit_code}]` array from `results` into the summary. Value: the operator's first file answers \"which one\", with data the process already holds. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-pool.cjs:977] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/orchestration-summary.json:1]\n\n3. **The failure-class rollup counts classes but cannot name a command, and the rerun command is not derivable from the summary alone.** The rollup (`buildFailureClassRollup`, `fanout-pool.cjs:998`) counts `quota`, `timeout` and the rest; the exact argv lives in `fanout-config.json`, which the summary does not copy. One concrete change: include `rerun_command` per failed lineage, built from the same `buildLineageDispatch` argv the run used (already available at `:4253`), with prompts replaced by their digest. Value: \"what do I type\" is answered without reconstructing flags. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-pool.cjs:998] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4253]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Requiring a new recovery command: the runner already holds every input a rerun needs, so the fix is serialization, not a new workflow.\n- Treating exit 2 as a deliberate safety stop: it protects the merge from partial input but gives the operator no merge at all, which is the opposite of the failure's cost.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for an `on_failure` branch in `step_fanout_spawn`: there is none, so the parent has no partial path to take.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"partially complete\" could mean some lineages failed or a lineage stopped early. Both are served by the same partial-merge change; the run-level `status` stays `error`/`partial` either way.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: the failed first attempt's summary was not committed; the exit-code and merge path are read from code.\n- Partial success: the node's question is answered by findings 1-3.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4253,4969`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-pool.cjs:977,998,1001`\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:432,2073`\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/orchestration-summary.json:1`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Questions addressed: partial-run summary (frontier node F-2-007)\n- Questions answered: yes, the node question: the summary names neither the lineage nor the command, and a partial run cannot reach synthesis at all.\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: following the exit code from the pool to the YAML found the missing merge path, which is a larger failure than the summary's missing labels.\n- What did not work and why: searching the committed summary for per-lineage fields found none because the writer never serializes `results`.\n- What I would do differently: read the writer and the pool return type together first; the discarded `results` array is the whole answer.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nClose F-2-007 as answered. Next: F-2-008 on dashboard per-node detail, then the restraint and design questions.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 6: Frontier node F-2-007 — what a partial fan-out tells the operator\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-2-007 (depth 2, child of F-1-002): does a partially complete fan-out summary name the failed lineage, its failure class and the exact command to rerun just that lineage?\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **A partial fan-out never reaches synthesis, so the successful lineages are never merged into a report.** `fanout-run.cjs:4969` exits `3` when every lineage failed and `2` when some failed; `deep-research.yaml`'s `step_fanout_spawn` has no `on_failure` branch and its next instruction is \\\"After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis\\\" (`:432`). One failed lane therefore stops the parent before `step_fanout_merge`, and the operator gets complete per-lineage artifacts but no consolidated `research.md` or registry. One concrete change: exit `0` with `status: \\\"partial\\\"` (or add `--allow-partial`) when at least one lineage succeeded, and let `phase_synthesis` merge what exists with a banner naming the failed labels. Value: a 2-of-3 fan-out still produces the deliverable it already paid for. Effort M. Risk medium (a partial merge must never read as complete coverage; the banner and summary counters are the guard). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4969] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:432] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:2073]\\n\\n2. **The per-lineage result already exists and is thrown away when the summary is written.** `buildPoolSummary` returns `{results, summary}` (`fanout-pool.cjs:977-1001`), and each result carries the lane output and its failure object; `writeOrchestrationSummary` serializes only the aggregate summary plus the fanout-specific fields, which is why the committed `orchestration-summary.json` has counts but no labels. One concrete change: write a reduced `lineages: [{label, status, reason, failure_class, exit_code}]` array from `results` into the summary. Value: the operator's first file answers \\\"which one\\\", with data the process already holds. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-pool.cjs:977] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/orchestration-summary.json:1]\\n\\n3. **The failure-class rollup counts classes but cannot name a command, and the rerun command is not derivable from the summary alone.** The rollup (`buildFailureClassRollup`, `fanout-pool.cjs:998`) counts `quota`, `timeout` and the rest; the exact argv lives in `fanout-config.json`, which the summary does not copy. One concrete change: include `rerun_command` per failed lineage, built from the same `buildLineageDispatch` argv the run used (already available at `:4253`), with prompts replaced by their digest. Value: \\\"what do I type\\\" is answered without reconstructing flags. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-pool.cjs:998] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4253]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Requiring a new recovery command: the runner already holds every input a rerun needs, so the fix is serialization, not a new workflow.\\n- Treating exit 2 as a deliberate safety stop: it protects the merge from partial input but gives the operator no merge at all, which is the opposite of the failure's cost.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for an `on_failure` branch in `step_fanout_spawn`: there is none, so the parent has no partial path to take.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"partially complete\\\" could mean some lineages failed or a lineage stopped early. Both are served by the same partial-merge change; the run-level `status` stays `error`/`partial` either way.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\\n- Missing dependencies: the failed first attempt's summary was not committed; the exit-code and merge path are read from code.\\n- Partial success: the node's question is answered by findings 1-3.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4253,4969`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-pool.cjs:977,998,1001`\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:432,2073`\\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/review/orchestration-summary.json:1`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 1.0\\n- Questions addressed: partial-run summary (frontier node F-2-007)\\n- Questions answered: yes, the node question: the summary names neither the lineage nor the command, and a partial run cannot reach synthesis at all.\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: following the exit code from the pool to the YAML found the missing merge path, which is a larger failure than the summary's missing labels.\\n- What did not work and why: searching the committed summary for per-lineage fields found none because the writer never serializes `results`.\\n- What I would do differently: read the writer and the pool return type together first; the discarded `results` array is the whole answer.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nClose F-2-007 as answered. Next: F-2-008 on dashboard per-node detail, then the restraint and design questions.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795138090676,"end":1795138095067}}}}
