{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795138200342,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f6931f79002HiPg6SMKTzVyJb","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f69315f0001QsCEeaYbQFvdGi","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-825638f47726c8e3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"D-011-10\" -A 18 specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md | head -40"},"output":"68:| D-011-10 | REQ-007 and AC-008 are amended: an accepted review pivot candidate becomes the next review focus and adds no frontier node. | Admitting it needed a reworked pivot transaction: a minimum seed spends the whole depth-1 band, so a new depth-1 node would close `exhausted:budget` on the next reduce; pivot candidates carry no scope for the relevance check; and `all_dimensions_clean` forms before `frontier_drained`. The operator's ruling allowed this fallback. | Implement admission of pivot candidates and restore the old REQ-007 wording. |\n69-| D-011-11 | Under expansive depth the review stuck count is per active node; a node-bound pass that recorded a new finding is progress; a node closed exhausted or blocked short of its dimensions files blocked search debt that does not hold the stop. | Clean passes on sibling nodes closed nodes that still owed dimensions, and the ratio shrinks as the run grows, so a pass with a new finding read as no progress; debt of 0 hid a node closed short. | Drop the nodeId option from deriveLoopCounters and the blocked-debt filing in the reducer. |\n70-| D-011-12 | One allow-list predicate, isEvidenceBearingIteration (complete, insight, stuck, or no status), decides frontier visits and dimension coverage in both loops and the convergence evidence filter. | A thought iteration spent node depth and covered a dimension; neither spec justifies a difference between the loops. | Restore the failed-status deny-list in frontier-admit.cjs. |\n71-| D-011-13 | Under expansive depth, step_frontier_scope writes a commit-range target's touched files (`git diff --name-only <range> -- <pathspec>`) into reviewScopeFiles; default runs are unchanged. | No step recorded them, so each leaf improvised and relevance admitted any scope. | Remove step_frontier_scope and the `scope` command. |\n72-| D-011-14 | A cli-claude-code fan-out lineage keeps acceptEdits by default; the operator opts into bypassPermissions with the `--sandbox-mode=` executor-group flag. A lineage is fulfilled only with iteration state, a terminal stop row from its attempt and every iteration row before that terminal row in the file. | Silently escalating permissions is the riskier default; a lineage that could not run Bash exited 0 and was counted fulfilled, and a lineage that skipped its stop gates was too; iteration stamps are model-written, so order is judged by file position. | Drop the completion check and the flag mapping. |\n73-| D-011-15 | A review fan-out skips the settle-time description.json refresh. | No doc set a mode for that refresh, and a review writes only its artifact dir. | Remove the review skip in the runner's metadata refresh. |\n74-<!-- /ANCHOR:build-decisions -->\n75-\n76----\n77-\n78-<!-- ANCHOR:operator-answers-verbatim -->\n79-## Appendix: Verbatim Operator Answers\n80-\n81-Each appendix item uses the same id as its operator decision. The options are included so the record preserves the full offered choice set.\n82-\n83-### Q001\n84-<!-- source: claude:94a4cf06-5c71-4a49-952f-6bbffe1f9b56:toolu_01GXZervRj4ta5M1vXJ4deg8:2 -->\n85-\n86-Question:\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"68:| D-011-10 | REQ-007 and AC-008 are amended: an accepted review pivot candidate becomes the next review focus and adds no frontier node. | Admitting it needed a reworked pivot transaction: a minimum seed spends the whole depth-1 band, so a new depth-1 node would close `exhausted:budget` on the next reduce; pivot candidates carry no scope for the relevance check; and `all_dimensions_clean` forms before `frontier_drained`. The operator's ruling allowed this fallback. | Implement admission of pivot candidates and restore the old REQ-007 wording. |\n69-| D-011-11 | Under expansive depth the review stuck count is per active node; a node-bound pass that recorded a new finding is progress; a node closed exhausted or blocked short of its dimensions files blocked search debt that does not hold the stop. | Clean passes on sibling nodes closed nodes that still owed dimensions, and the ratio shrinks as the run grows, so a pass with a new finding read as no progress; debt of 0 hid a node closed short. | Drop the nodeId option from deriveLoopCounters and the blocked-debt filing in the reducer. |\n70-| D-011-12 | One allow-list predicate, isEvidenceBearingIteration (complete, insight, stuck, or no status), decides frontier visits and dimension coverage in both loops and the convergence evidence filter. | A thought iteration spent node depth and covered a dimension; neither spec justifies a difference between the loops. | Restore the failed-status deny-list in frontier-admit.cjs. |\n71-| D-011-13 | Under expansive depth, step_frontier_scope writes a commit-range target's touched files (`git diff --name-only <range> -- <pathspec>`) into reviewScopeFiles; default runs are unchanged. | No step recorded them, so each leaf improvised and relevance admitted any scope. | Remove step_frontier_scope and the `scope` command. |\n72-| D-011-14 | A cli-claude-code fan-out lineage keeps acceptEdits by default; the operator opts into bypassPermissions with the `--sandbox-mode=` executor-group flag. A lineage is fulfilled only with iteration state, a terminal stop row from its attempt and every iteration row before that terminal row in the file. | Silently escalating permissions is the riskier default; a lineage that could not run Bash exited 0 and was counted fulfilled, and a lineage that skipped its stop gates was too; iteration stamps are model-written, so order is judged by file position. | Drop the completion check and the flag mapping. |\n73-| D-011-15 | A review fan-out skips the settle-time description.json refresh. | No doc set a mode for that refresh, and a review writes only its artifact dir. | Remove the review skip in the runner's metadata refresh. |\n74-<!-- /ANCHOR:build-decisions -->\n75-\n76----\n77-\n78-<!-- ANCHOR:operator-answers-verbatim -->\n79-## Appendix: Verbatim Operator Answers\n80-\n81-Each appendix item uses the same id as its operator decision. The options are included so the record preserves the full offered choice set.\n82-\n83-### Q001\n84-<!-- source: claude:94a4cf06-5c71-4a49-952f-6bbffe1f9b56:toolu_01GXZervRj4ta5M1vXJ4deg8:2 -->\n85-\n86-Question:\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"D-011-10\\\" -A 18 specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1795138199417,"end":1795138200342}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795138200450,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f693205e001EKh4iclRH7mpFO","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f69315f0001QsCEeaYbQFvdGi","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1d2480b4ca51bc4","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\"), path=require(\"path\");\nconst root=\"specs/system-deep-loop\";\nconst hits=[];\nfunction walk(d){for(const e of fs.readdirSync(d,{withFileTypes:true})){const p=path.join(d,e.name); if(e.isDirectory()){if(e.name===\"node_modules\")continue; walk(p);} else if(e.name===\"deep-research-state.jsonl\"){hits.push(p);}}}\nwalk(root);\nlet legacy=0, withTerm=0;\nfor(const p of hits){let rows=[];try{rows=fs.readFileSync(p,\"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean).map(JSON.parse)}catch{continue}\n const terms=rows.filter(r=>r.type===\"event\"&&[\"synthesis_complete\",\"phase_synthesis_complete\",\"synthesis\",\"synthesis_incomplete\"].includes(r.event));\n if(terms.length===0) legacy++; else withTerm++;\n}\nconsole.log(\"state logs\",hits.length,\"legacy(no terminal)\",legacy,\"with terminal\",withTerm);\nconsole.log(hits.filter(p=>{try{const rows=fs.readFileSync(p,\"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean).map(JSON.parse);return rows.filter(r=>r.type===\"event\"&&[\"synthesis_complete\",\"phase_synthesis_complete\",\"synthesis\",\"synthesis_incomplete\"].includes(r.event)).length===0}catch{return false}}).slice(0,8).join(\"\\n\"));\n'"},"output":"state logs 104 legacy(no terminal) 42 with terminal 61\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/001-deep-loop-innovation/001-research-inputs-and-architecture/001-deep-loop-market-research/research/deep-research-state.jsonl\nspecs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/001-deep-loop-innovation/001-research-inputs-and-architecture/002-deep-loop-effectiveness-and-fanout/research/deep-re