{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795138204762,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f69331bb00111V7LPmVT5VXR0","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f69326eb0016IpJZbFZ0WDenw","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfb684277d440608","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\"), path=require(\"path\");\nconst root=\"specs/system-deep-loop\";const hits=[];\nfunction walk(d){for(const e of fs.readdirSync(d,{withFileTypes:true})){const p=path.join(d,e.name); if(e.isDirectory()){if(e.name===\"node_modules\")continue; walk(p);} else if(e.name===\"deep-research-state.jsonl\"){hits.push(p);}}}\nwalk(root);\nlet legacyWithReport=0, legacyNoReport=0;\nfor(const p of hits){let rows=[];try{rows=fs.readFileSync(p,\"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean).map(JSON.parse)}catch{continue}\n const terms=rows.filter(r=>r.type===\"event\"&&[\"synthesis_complete\",\"phase_synthesis_complete\",\"synthesis\",\"synthesis_incomplete\"].includes(r.event));\n if(terms.length>0)continue;\n const dir=path.dirname(p);const report=path.join(dir,\"research.md\");\n if(fs.existsSync(report))legacyWithReport++;else legacyNoReport++;\n}\nconsole.log(\"legacy with research.md\",legacyWithReport,\"legacy without\",legacyNoReport);\n'"},"output":"legacy with research.md 31 legacy without 11\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"legacy with research.md 31 legacy without 11\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && node -e '\\nconst fs=require(\\\"fs\\\"), path=require(\\\"path\\\");\\nconst root=\\\"specs/system-deep-loop\\\";const hits=[];\\nfunction walk(d){for(const e of fs.readdirSync(d,{withFileTypes:true})){const p=path.join(d,e.name); if(e.isDirectory()){if(e.name===\\\"node_modules\\\")continue; walk(p);} else if(e.name===\\\"deep-research-state.jsonl\\\"){hits.push(p);}}}\\nwalk(root);\\nlet legacyWithReport=0, legacyNoReport=0;\\nfor(const p of hits){let rows=[];try{rows=fs.readFileSync(p,\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\n\\\").filter(Boolean).map(JSON.parse)}catch{continue}\\n const terms=rows.filter(r=>r.type===\\\"event\\\"&&[\\\"synthesis_complete\\\",\\\"phase_synthesis_complete\\\",\\\"synthesis\\\",\\\"synthesis_incomplete\\\"].includes(r.event));\\n if(terms.length>0)continue;\\n const dir=path.dirname(p);const report=path.join(dir,\\\"research.md\\\");\\n if(fs.existsSync(report))legacyWithReport++;else legacyNoReport++;\\n}\\nconsole.log(\\\"legacy with research.md\\\",legacyWithReport,\\\"legacy without\\\",legacyNoReport);\\n'\"}"},"time":{"start":1795138204091,"end":1795138204762}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1795138205667,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"id":"prt_1f69337e3001sZ5oM9UR5uhNqB","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f69326eb0016IpJZbFZ0WDenw","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"5551331278ce14745ac9c6f136efae3ebb255aae","cost":0.001878312,"tokens":{"input":2081,"output":327,"reasoning":140,"cache":{"read":272128,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795138207610,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"id":"prt_1f6933f7a001OLCHnpzdrCsGN0","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f69337e9001qbEhSlwTYAHeBg","type":"step-start","snapshot":"5551331278ce14745ac9c6f136efae3ebb255aae"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795138215298,"sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","part":{"partID":"prt_1f693472c001YnVw57BdD2Ufek","sessionID":"ses_e09762d57ffewQMol0oGMct7ei","messageID":"msg_1f69337e9001qbEhSlwTYAHeBg","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c2bc69d99fc6937","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 9: Q5 — stuck scoping, completion for older runs, and a cheap pivot admission\n\n## Focus\n\nQ5 design questions: (a) should research count stuck passes per frontier node as review now does; (b) does the lineage completion check break resume and extend for older committed research lineages, and what is the right rule; (c) is there a cheap design that makes pivot admission into the frontier work?\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Research still counts stuck passes lineage-wide: `nodeScoped` is gated on `loopType === 'review'`.** `convergence.cjs:1775-1778` sets `nodeScoped` only for review, so a research run with an active node counts every low-novelty pass in the lineage, and the workflow then closes the active node as `exhausted/stuck`. The review decision record already settled the principle (D-011-11: a node-bound pass that recorded a new finding is progress, and clean sibling passes must not close a node). One concrete change: drop the loop-type gate and add `frontier.activeNodeId` (and `activeNextDimension`) to the research projection via the shared frontier module from iteration 8. Value: research nodes close on their own evidence, not their siblings'. Effort S/M. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1775] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1406] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:69]\n\n2. **The completion check fails 31 committed research lineages that have a `research.md` but no terminal closeout row.** A scan of `specs/system-deep-loop/**/deep-research-state.jsonl` finds 104 state logs, 42 with no terminal synthesis event, and 31 of those 42 have `research.md` on disk. `TERMINAL_STOP_EVENTS_BY_LOOP_TYPE.research` requires one of `synthesis_complete`, `phase_synthesis_complete`, `synthesis` or `synthesis_incomplete` (`fanout-run.cjs:1248-1251`), and `checkLineageCompletion` fails `no_terminal_event` when none is present (`lineage-timestamp-window.ts:202-208`). The prompt's \"3 of 12\" understates the break; the measured population is 31 with a report. One concrete change: keep the terminal-row requirement for a live attempt, and fall back to `completionFromArtifacts` (already implemented at `fanout-run.cjs:1282`) when the lineage config is `status: complete` and the log holds no terminal row at all. Value: historical audit and re-run stop mislabelling finished work. Effort S. Risk low (the live path is untouched). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1248] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts:202] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1282]\n\n3. **Resume and extend are not broken; only the audit of a *historical* run is.** A resume or extend re-runs `phase_synthesis`, whose `step_convergence_report` always hands a fresh closeout row to the gateway (`deep-research.yaml:2199-2225`), so the current attempt satisfies the terminal check. The break is confined to code paths that judge a completed run without re-running it, which is exactly the fallback in finding 2. One concrete change: name the two rules in the completion helper's contract (\"current attempt: terminal row required; historical completed run: report artifact accepted\"). Value: stops a future reader from weakening the live check to fix the audit. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:2199] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts:169]\n\n4. **Pivot admission has a cheap design: carry the saturated focus's scope, admit pivots without the relevance check, reserve one depth-1 slot, and order `frontier_drained` before `all_dimensions_clean`.** D-011-10 rejected admission for three structural reasons: a minimum seed spends the whole depth-1 band so a new depth-1 node closes `exhausted:budget` on the next reduce; pivot candidates carry no scope for the relevance check; and `all_dimensions_clean` forms before `frontier_drained`. Each has a small answer: copy the previous focus's `scope` onto the pivot node (the saturated direction already has one) and tag it `origin: pivot` so admission skips only the relevance check; reserve one depth-1 slot by subtracting `1 / maxIterations` from `budgetSplit.depth1` when the pivot branch is enabled; and evaluate the frontier-terminal gate before the clean-stop candidate in `convergence.cjs`. Value: REQ-007's promise can be kept without a reworked pivot transaction. Effort M. Risk medium (the reservation changes band arithmetic and needs a test). [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:68] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:613] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1158]\n\n5. **The reducer copies a leaf's `Recommended Next Focus` narrative into Next Focus verbatim, even when it is an instruction rather than a question.** With the frontier terminal, `deriveNextFocusFromContinuity` takes `latestLeafNextFocus` (`reduce-state.cjs:2574-2588`); this run's Next Focus became \"Close F-2-008 as answered…\", so the next iteration would have chased a closing instruction had this pass not overridden it. One concrete change: when the frontier has no open node, prefer the first unchecked key question over the leaf recommendation, and reject a recommendation that does not end in a question mark or name a scope. Value: the loop always works a question. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2574] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:151]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Weakening the live completion check to fix the audit: a live attempt that writes nothing must still fail, so the fallback has to be scoped to a completed historical config.\n- Admitting pivot candidates with a full reworked transaction: the three D-011-10 blockers each have a one-line answer; a transaction rewrite is not needed.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for a research `activeNodeId` in the registry: the research projection does not emit one, which is why the node-scoped counter cannot be enabled by a flag alone.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"break resume and extend\" could mean the live path or the historical audit. Both are separated in findings 2 and 3.\n- Contradictory evidence: the prompt's \"3 of 12\" vs the measured 31 of 104 with a report. The measurement wins; the discrepancy is recorded here rather than smoothed over.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1158,1406,1775`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1248,1282`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts:169,202`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:613`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2574`\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:2199`\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:68`\n- Scan of `specs/system-deep-loop/**/deep-research-state.jsonl` (104 logs)\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Questions addressed: Q5 (a), (b), (c) and the next-focus consumer\n- Questions answered: Q5: research stuck scoping is a one-gate change; the completion break is 31 historical reports, not a live resume/extend break; pivot admission has a three-part cheap design.\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: scanning the committed state logs turned a remembered \"3 of 12\" into a measured 31 of 104 with a report, which changes the severity and the right fix.\n- What did not work and why: looking for a research active-node field found none, so the stuck-scoping fix is two-part rather than one line.\n- What I would do differently: run the population scan before reasoning about backward compatibility; the corpus is the evidence.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nQ6 prior art on the web, then synthesis.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 9: Q5 — stuck scoping, completion for older runs, and a cheap pivot admission\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nQ5 design questions: (a) should research count stuck passes per frontier node as review now does; (b) does the lineage completion check break resume and extend for older committed research lineages, and what is the right rule; (c) is there a cheap design that makes pivot admission into the frontier work?\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **Research still counts stuck passes lineage-wide: `nodeScoped` is gated on `loopType === 'review'`.** `convergence.cjs:1775-1778` sets `nodeScoped` only for review, so a research run with an active node counts every low-novelty pass in the lineage, and the workflow then closes the active node as `exhausted/stuck`. The review decision record already settled the principle (D-011-11: a node-bound pass that recorded a new finding is progress, and clean sibling passes must not close a node). One concrete change: drop the loop-type gate and add `frontier.activeNodeId` (and `activeNextDimension`) to the research projection via the shared frontier module from iteration 8. Value: research nodes close on their own evidence, not their siblings'. Effort S/M. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1775] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1406] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:69]\\n\\n2. **The completion check fails 31 committed research lineages that have a `research.md` but no terminal closeout row.** A scan of `specs/system-deep-loop/**/deep-research-state.jsonl` finds 104 state logs, 42 with no terminal synthesis event, and 31 of those 42 have `research.md` on disk. `TERMINAL_STOP_EVENTS_BY_LOOP_TYPE.research` requires one of `synthesis_complete`, `phase_synthesis_complete`, `synthesis` or `synthesis_incomplete` (`fanout-run.cjs:1248-1251`), and `checkLineageCompletion` fails `no_terminal_event` when none is present (`lineage-timestamp-window.ts:202-208`). The prompt's \\\"3 of 12\\\" understates the break; the measured population is 31 with a report. One concrete change: keep the terminal-row requirement for a live attempt, and fall back to `completionFromArtifacts` (already implemented at `fanout-run.cjs:1282`) when the lineage config is `status: complete` and the log holds no terminal row at all. Value: historical audit and re-run stop mislabelling finished work. Effort S. Risk low (the live path is untouched). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1248] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts:202] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1282]\\n\\n3. **Resume and extend are not broken; only the audit of a *historical* run is.** A resume or extend re-runs `phase_synthesis`, whose `step_convergence_report` always hands a fresh closeout row to the gateway (`deep-research.yaml:2199-2225`), so the current attempt satisfies the terminal check. The break is confined to code paths that judge a completed run without re-running it, which is exactly the fallback in finding 2. One concrete change: name the two rules in the completion helper's contract (\\\"current attempt: terminal row required; historical completed run: report artifact accepted\\\"). Value: stops a future reader from weakening the live check to fix the audit. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:2199] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts:169]\\n\\n4. **Pivot admission has a cheap design: carry the saturated focus's scope, admit pivots without the relevance check, reserve one depth-1 slot, and order `frontier_drained` before `all_dimensions_clean`.** D-011-10 rejected admission for three structural reasons: a minimum seed spends the whole depth-1 band so a new depth-1 node closes `exhausted:budget` on the next reduce; pivot candidates carry no scope for the relevance check; and `all_dimensions_clean` forms before `frontier_drained`. Each has a small answer: copy the previous focus's `scope` onto the pivot node (the saturated direction already has one) and tag it `origin: pivot` so admission skips only the relevance check; reserve one depth-1 slot by subtracting `1 / maxIterations` from `budgetSplit.depth1` when the pivot branch is enabled; and evaluate the frontier-terminal gate before the clean-stop candidate in `convergence.cjs`. Value: REQ-007's promise can be kept without a reworked pivot transaction. Effort M. Risk medium (the reservation changes band arithmetic and needs a test). [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:68] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:613] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1158]\\n\\n5. **The reducer copies a leaf's `Recommended Next Focus` narrative into Next Focus verbatim, even when it is an instruction rather than a question.** With the frontier terminal, `deriveNextFocusFromContinuity` takes `latestLeafNextFocus` (`reduce-state.cjs:2574-2588`); this run's Next Focus became \\\"Close F-2-008 as answered…\\\", so the next iteration would have chased a closing instruction had this pass not overridden it. One concrete change: when the frontier has no open node, prefer the first unchecked key question over the leaf recommendation, and reject a recommendation that does not end in a question mark or name a scope. Value: the loop always works a question. Effort S. Risk low. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2574] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:151]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Weakening the live completion check to fix the audit: a live attempt that writes nothing must still fail, so the fallback has to be scoped to a completed historical config.\\n- Admitting pivot candidates with a full reworked transaction: the three D-011-10 blockers each have a one-line answer; a transaction rewrite is not needed.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for a research `activeNodeId` in the registry: the research projection does not emit one, which is why the node-scoped counter cannot be enabled by a flag alone.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"break resume and extend\\\" could mean the live path or the historical audit. Both are separated in findings 2 and 3.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the prompt's \\\"3 of 12\\\" vs the measured 31 of 104 with a report. The measurement wins; the discrepancy is recorded here rather than smoothed over.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs:1158,1406,1775`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:1248,1282`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts:169,202`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs:613`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2574`\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:2199`\\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:68`\\n- Scan of `specs/system-deep-loop/**/deep-research-state.jsonl` (104 logs)\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 1.0\\n- Questions addressed: Q5 (a), (b), (c) and the next-focus consumer\\n- Questions answered: Q5: research stuck scoping is a one-gate change; the completion break is 31 historical reports, not a live resume/extend break; pivot admission has a three-part cheap design.\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: scanning the committed state logs turned a remembered \\\"3 of 12\\\" into a measured 31 of 104 with a report, which changes the severity and the right fix.\\n- What did not work and why: looking for a research active-node field found none, so the stuck-scoping fix is two-part rather than one line.\\n- What I would do differently: run the population scan before reasoning about backward compatibility; the corpus is the evidence.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nQ6 prior art on the web, then synthesis.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795138209580,"end":1795138215298}}}}
